{"text": "EXHIBIT 4\n\nCOMPARISON OF BARCLAY KS TAR DELIVERIES WITH CAMBRIDGE,\nCARLTON, AND NOW UNDER CONDITIONS WHERE BARCLAY\n\u2018NICOTINE DELIVERY 18 1.5 TIMES RIGHER\n\nABSTRACT\nCotinine levels in blood show that average nicotine absorption by\nregular 1 mg tar sooker\u00e9 smoking Barclay KS is 1.5 tines higher than\naverage nicotine absorption of 1 mg tar smokers smoking Carlton or\nCambridge. Machine smoking reeulte from BEN, R. J. Reynolds, and\nPhilip Morris over a range of possible hunan emoking conditions show\nthat at 1.5 times higher nicotine deliveries, Barclay KS delivers on\naverage 1.14 times the tar of Carlton, Cambridge, and Now. For\nexample, Sf Barclay KS delivers 6 mg of tar to the consumer, Cambridge\nKS, Carlton XS, and Now KS will deliver about 5 mg.\nThis note presents the experimental date and shows the procedures\n\nused to ascertain the relative tar deliveries.\n\nRESULTS AND DISCUSSION\nResults are summarized in Table 1. It shows Cambridge, Carlton,\nand Now tar deliveries for several Barclay tar deliveries in the 3-7\nmg range. In each case, the Barclay nicotine delivery is 1.5 times\n\nhigher than that of the competitive brand.\n\n980802T0S",
